  <content>
    <!-- Simplified maintenance-planning structure: scheduling / mpSystem / mpSystemChap /
         mpSection are used here as plausible stand-ins; the author was not fully certain of
         the schedul.xsd schema's exact element names. See README for this judgement call. -->
    <scheduling>
      <mpSystem>
        <mpSystemChap>
          <title>Array Module Maintenance Plan</title>
          <mpSection>
            <title>On-Condition Replacement</title>
            <para>Replace the array module on a confirmed BIT failure (fault code MRAD-ARR-0417).
            See the fault isolation data for the isolation steps and the remove and install
            procedures below for the replacement task.</para>
            <dmRef>
              <dmRefIdent>
                <dmCode modelIdentCode="ODMRAD" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="34"
                        subSystemCode="1" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="01"
                        disassyCode="00" disassyCodeVariant="A"
                        infoCode="520" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="A"/>
              </dmRefIdent>
            </dmRef>
            <dmRef>
              <dmRefIdent>
                <dmCode modelIdentCode="ODMRAD" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="34"
                        subSystemCode="1" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="01"
                        disassyCode="00" disassyCodeVariant="A"
                        infoCode="720" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="A"/>
              </dmRefIdent>
            </dmRef>
          </mpSection>
          <mpSection>
            <title>Periodic Array Inspection</title>
            <limit>
              <threshold thresholdUnitOfMeasure="days">
                <thresholdValue>180</thresholdValue>
              </threshold>
            </limit>
            <para>Every 180 days, inspect the array face for physical damage and inspect each
            array module connector for corrosion or looseness.</para>
          </mpSection>
        </mpSystemChap>
      </mpSystem>
    </scheduling>
